## Step 2 — "Configure DHCP Relay on the DUT interface connected to the client to use the upstream DHCPv6 server" → expected "Client successfully obtains an IPv6 address lease from the server via the DUT; client has a correct IPv6 address." (17:11:32–17:12:27; evidence/5093/5093-s2cfg-u5.out, -s2b-eth1.out/.pcap)
```
IE520-stk(config)#interface vlan3993
IE520-stk(config-if)#ip dhcp-relay server-address 2001:db8:5093:10::2 vlan10      (no % line)
show running-config interface vlan3993:
 interface vlan3993
  ipv6 address 2001:db8:5093:1::1/64
  ipv6 enable
  ip dhcp-relay server-address 2001:db8:5093:10::2 vlan10
show ip dhcp-relay interface vlan3993: vlan3993 is up, line protocol is up ... List of servers : 2001:db8:5093:10::2
```
First attempt, 17:11:50 (evidence/5093/5093-s2-eth1.out/.pcap). The client reported "no ADVERTISE",
but its own capture holds three ADVERTISEs from the relay (fe80::200:cdff:fe37:d6f → the client),
one per SOLICIT, each with the matching xid (0x509360 …) and IA_NA 2001:db8:5093:1::1cb. Cause: a tool
defect. scapy's `AsyncSniffer.results` is only filled at `stop()`, so the client's wait loop never
saw them. It was fixed with a `prn=` callback (tools/dhc6.py as committed) and re-run:
```
17:12:26.219 [step2b] SOLICIT 1/3 xid 0x5095a0 fe80::f667:7041:7dff:3cfc -> ff02::1:2
17:12:26.220 [step2b] ADVERTISE xid 0x5095a0 from fe80::200:cdff:fe37:d6f (00:00:cd:37:0d:6f) server-duid 00010001324f140c0000cd400394 addrs [('2001:db8:5093:1::1cb', 604800, 2592000)]
17:12:26.275 [step2b] REQUEST xid 0x5095a1 for ['2001:db8:5093:1::1cb']
17:12:26.376 [step2b] REPLY xid 0x5095a1 from fe80::200:cdff:fe37:d6f (00:00:cd:37:0d:6f) addrs [('2001:db8:5093:1::1cb', 604800, 2592000)]
17:12:26.376 [step2b] LEASE 2001:db8:5093:1::1cb preferred 604800 valid 2592000
17:12:26.904 [step2b] RESULT rc=0 (LEASED)
```
The server DUID 0001 0001 … 0000cd400394 is DUID-LLT with the 4050's MAC (00:00:cd:40:03:94). The
answers come from the relay's link-local on vlan3993, with the stack MAC 00:00:cd:37:0d:6f, so they
came through the DUT. 2001:db8:5093:1::1cb lies in the pool range and in vlan3993's
2001:db8:5093:1::/64. The host installed nothing: the address was checked in the REPLY and in the
server's binding (step 3), not configured on eth1.
⇒ Step 2 as expected.

## Step 3 — "Check counts of relay transactions in 'show count dns-relay'" → expected "Output shows counts of requests, replies and relays to clients and servers" (17:12:41–17:12:52; evidence/5093/5093-s3-u5.out, -s3-u1.out)
The case text's `show count dns-relay` is a typo. The AW+ command is `show counter dhcp-relay`.
```
IE520-stk#show counter dhcp-relay
DHCP relay counters
Requests In ....... 0   Replies In ....... 0   Relayed To Server ....... 0   Relayed To Client ....... 0   (IPv4; all other v4 counters 0)
