DHCPv6 Replies In       ....... 5
DHCPv6 Relayed To Server ....... 5
DHCPv6 Relayed To Client ....... 5
4050-5g#show counter ipv6 dhcp-server
SOLICIT in 4   ADVERTISE out 4   REQUEST in 1   REPLY out 1   RELAY FORWARD in 5   (others 0)
4050-5g#show ipv6 dhcp binding
Pool ck5093
 Address 2001:db8:5093:1::1cb
         client IAID 00005093, DUID 0003000100f04d007716
         preferred lifetime 604800, valid lifetime 2592000
         starts  at 30 Sep 2026 17:12:24 / expires at 30 Oct 2026 17:12:24
stack show ipv6 neighbors: 2001:db8:5093:10::2 0000.cd40.0394 vlan10 sa1; fe80::f667:7041:7dff:3cfc 00f0.4d00.7716 vlan3993 port3.0.13
```
5 = 3 SOLICITs from the first step-2 attempt + 1 SOLICIT + 1 REQUEST from the re-run, each relayed
both ways. The server's four SOLICITs and one REQUEST all arrived as RELAY-FORW (RELAY FORWARD in 5).
The DUID 0003 0001 00f04d007716 is DUID-LL with tb470 eth1's MAC, as the client sent it.
⇒ Step 3 as expected.

