## Observation O-1 carried from T5082 (not graded here)
T5082 saw the 4050 send ADVERTISE out on vlan10 while the DUT's own DHCPv6 client counted
ADVERTISE in 0. The relay path in this case crosses the same stack vlan10 / sa1 / 4050 vlan10 link.
Every server message was delivered and processed. The DUT counted DHCPv6 Replies In 5, then 4 after
the reboot, with Relayed To Client equal each time, and the client received every one. The server's
replies to a relay go to the relay agent's address on UDP 547 (RFC 8415). They were counted, but not
captured on the wire, since there is no capture point on vlan10. So the T5082 loss is
NOT a general failure of DHCPv6 from the 4050 to the DUT over that link, and not the 4050's server
config. What T5082 exercised and this case did not is the DUT's own client receive path (UDP 546,
to its link-local). That path remains the open candidate. Not investigated further (outside T5093).

## Teardown (17:20:50–17:23:47; evidence/5093/5093-td-u5.out, -td-del*-u5.out, -td-u1.out)
- Stack: `boot config-file flash:/tb470-bench.cfg` (synchronised to members 1 and 4); port3.0.13
  `no switchport access vlan`; vlan3993 `no ip dhcp-relay server-address …`, `no ipv6 address …`, `no
  ipv6 enable`; vlan10 `no ipv6 address …`, `no ipv6 enable`; `vlan database` `no vlan 3993`. No `% ` line.
- `delete flash:/ck5093.cfg`: the first attempt (17:22:2x) was declined. The prompt is
  `Delete flash:/ck5093.cfg?  (y/n)[n]:`, the driver's y/n regex did not allow the `[n]`, and its
  cleanup CR took the default `n`. The file stayed and the console was left at the exec prompt. The
  regex was fixed (tools/ckyn.py) and the delete re-run: `Deleting... Successful operation` on the
  master, then `delete IE520-stk-1/flash:/ck5093.cfg` and `delete IE520-stk-4/flash:/ck5093.cfg`, the
  same. The master's delete does not propagate to members. `dir` afterwards: only `tb470-bench.cfg`
  (2927 bytes, 03:07:49, unchanged) on members 3, 1 and 4.
- 4050: vlan10 `no ipv6 dhcp server`, `no ipv6 address …`, `no ipv6 enable`; `no ipv6 route
  2001:db8:5093:1::/64 2001:db8:5093:10::1`; `no ipv6 dhcp pool ck5093`. `show ipv6 dhcp pool` and
  `show ipv6 dhcp binding` are empty, and `show ipv6 dhcp interface` shows only `vlan1 is in client mode`.
- tb470: nothing was installed. The client is a scapy process that exited at the end of each run;
  no tcpdump was started. `ps` afterwards: no dhc6 or tcpdump process.

